  message: "Materialized from dogfood tranche 05 (F96.A2 / anon-card-006). Mechanism: main_function entrypoint kind is overloaded — its target node.kind splits function (9/11) vs file (2/11) and only the free-text label disambiguates. Evidence: frozen substrate.json (probe_2_ep.log, probe_2_mainfunc.log, probe_2_mainfunc2.log) — (main_function,function)=9, (main_function,file)=2 both conf=1.0 targeting __main__.py:1-1:file:file; spec line 351 example implies a function target. Fresh run: temp pkg/__main__.py with no main() yields target_kind=file conf=0.96. Magnitude: 2/11 main_function entrypoints, undocumented file-target case. Blind severity 3/5, reproduced on frozen substrate + fresh run. NOT_A_DUPLICATE — no existing item covers the file-target overload. RELATED to INV-hosuh (satisfied — entrypoint detection double-counts scripts with BOTH if __name__ AND main(); that handles the double-count, not the single-target file-vs-function kind overload) and WI-suvil (the confidence-drift secondary note, hardcoded-confidence family)."  # 00da
